From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ams: AD5X IFS endless spool follows Kiln's auto-refill

With Kiln OS's IFS driver (ifs.auto_refill published, no lessWaste or
bambufy plugin), Endless Spool is auto-refill: on or off from
auto_refill, "on, but nothing will switch" when no slot has a backup,
and switchable, so the Endless Spool switch in the filament system
settings sends IFS_AUTO_REFILL ENABLE=. The backups are the driver's
refill_backups (its refill_match rule: exact, similar or any colour);
each slot's nearest backup is the endless-spool relation the screen
shows, and only a listed slot counts as an eligible backup.

The runout pop-up on a paused print waits 180 s only when auto-refill
is on, the slot that ran out had a backup and no refill has run for
this runout yet; otherwise 30 s. Its text says whether auto-refill is
off, has no backup for the spool, or had one that did not take over.
The driver lists no backups for a slot without filament, so the slot
that ran out keeps the list it had.

Settings > Filament Auto-Refill (0010) is unchanged; both send the same
commands. Without auto_refill (older driver) nothing changes.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
---
